note: |
  Deliberately the mirror image of 03. Everything criterion 4's "10" asks for is
  present and visible in the diff: RLS enabled, granular per-operation policies with
  `with check` on both write paths, a pgTAP test that proves a stranger gets zero rows
  instead of asserting the policies exist, and an owner id that comes from
  `safeGetUser()` in the route rather than from the body or the path.

  It is also a false-positive probe for the other four criteria: the length cap lives
  in the migration with the zod side mirroring it and a comment saying which side owns
  it (1), nothing touches the generation path (2), the new branches are covered by
  boundary tests against the real schema rather than a mock (3), and the route stays
  thin while reusing `cvSaveErrorMessages`, `readBoundedJson` and `getCv` instead of
  duplicating them (5).

  A model that raises a finding here is speculating about code it was not shown —
  which is what this fixture measures, since REVIEW_INSTRUCTIONS dropped the blanket
  "never speculate" rule on 2026-08-26.
